import AxQM.Concrete.DipolarCoupling

/-!
# Concrete: refocusing the dipolar coupling into the `Z₁Z₂` (weak-coupling) form

This file formalises the **pulse-sequence content of Nielsen & Chuang, Exercise 7.40**
(*refocusing dipolar interactions*, p. 332): give a
sequence of pulses that turns the two-spin through-space dipolar coupling `H^D_{1,2}(n̂)`
(eq. 7.136, `Concrete/DipolarCoupling.lean`) into the much simpler weak-coupling form of (7.138),

`H^J_{12} ≈ (ℏ J / 4) · Z₁Z₂`.

## The physics, and how it is captured

Write the two-spin coupling in the Pauli basis. The dipolar bracket is
`σ⃗₁·σ⃗₂ − 3(σ⃗₁·n̂)(σ⃗₂·n̂) = ∑_{a,b} D_{ab} σ^a₁ σ^b₂` with `D_{ab} = δ_{ab} − 3 n_a n_b` the
traceless symmetric dipolar tensor. The target form keeps **only** the `Z₁Z₂` (`a = b = z`) term.
To isolate
it one refocuses with the two `180°` `ẑ`-rotation pulses `R²_{z1}` and `R²_{z2}` (eq. 7.149 with `ẑ`
in place of `x̂`): each is the propagator `exp(−iπZ/2) = −iZ`, so — exactly as in the refocusing
identity (7.150), where the two `−i` global phases cancel — **conjugating by the pulse equals
conjugating by the Pauli `Z`**. Interspersing the free dipolar evolution with these pulses realises
the four toggling frames

`{ I⊗I, Z⊗I, I⊗Z, Z⊗Z }`  (the `Z`-type Pauli group, generated by the two pulses),

and the resulting zeroth-order **average (toggling-frame) Hamiltonian** is the symmetric average
`H ↦ ¼ (H + Z₁ H Z₁ + Z₂ H Z₂ + Z₁Z₂ H Z₁Z₂)` — `zRefocusAverage` below. This average is the
projection onto the `Z`-diagonal Paulis: a Pauli survives iff it commutes with both `Z₁` and `Z₂`
(i.e. is a product of `I`/`Z` on each spin), so of `H^D`'s nine coupling terms only `Z₁Z₂` remains.
The upshot (`zRefocusAverage_dipolarCoupling`) is

`⟨H^D_{1,2}(n̂)⟩_pulses = (ℏ J_eff / 4) · Z₁Z₂`,  `J_eff = γ₁ γ₂ (1 − 3 n_z²) / r³`,

which is precisely the form (7.138), with the residual coupling the secular dipolar constant
`∝ (1 − 3 n_z²) = (1 − 3 cos²θ)`.

*Scope.* We formalise the zeroth-order average Hamiltonian that the pulse cycle produces — the
standard, and physically operative, level of the "sequence of pulses" answer. The higher-order
Magnus corrections / the exact multi-period propagator (a short-cycle limit) are deliberately not
claimed here.

## Setting

Everything here is stated for matrices (`Matrix`, the Pauli matrices, `Kronecker`, `Concrete`'s
`dipolarCoupling`/`dipolarBracket`/`spinSpinCoupling`/`spinDirProduct`). Compare
`Concrete/DipolarCoupling.lean` (Exercise 7.35) and `Concrete/Refocusing.lean` (Exercise 7.38).
These are the statements of N&C Exercise 7.40 (`AxQM/NC/Ch7/Exercise7_40.lean`).

## The declarations

* `diagPart A = ½ (A + Z A Z)` — the single-spin `Z`-diagonal part, the average over `{I, Z}`; with
  `diagPart X = diagPart Y = 0`, `diagPart Z = Z`, and `diagPart (n·σ) = n_z Z`.
* `refocusZ₁ = Z⊗I`, `refocusZ₂ = I⊗Z`, `refocusZ₁₂ = Z⊗Z` — the `ẑ`-refocusing pulses (`Z⊗Z` is
  their product, `refocusZ₁_mul_refocusZ₂`), each a Hermitian unitary involution.
* `zRefocusAverage H` — the toggling-frame average over the four pulses, ℂ-linear
  (`zRefocusAverage_add`/`_smul`/`_sub`) with the key structural identity
  `zRefocusAverage (A⊗B) = diagPart A ⊗ diagPart B` (`zRefocusAverage_kronecker`).
* `zRefocusAverage_spinSpinCoupling = Z⊗Z`, `zRefocusAverage_spinDirProduct n = n_z² • (Z⊗Z)`,
  `zRefocusAverage_dipolarBracket n = (1 − 3 n_z²) • (Z⊗Z)`.
* `dipolarEffectiveCoupling` and **Exercise 7.40 itself**, `zRefocusAverage_dipolarCoupling`:
  `⟨H^D_{1,2}⟩_pulses = (ℏ J_eff / 4) • (Z⊗Z)`, the form (7.138).
-/

namespace AxQM.Concrete

open Matrix
open scoped Kronecker BigOperators

/-! ### The single-spin `Z`-diagonal part `diagPart A = ½(A + ZAZ)` -/

/-- The **`Z`-diagonal part** of a single-spin operator, `diagPart A = ½ (A + Z A Z)`: the average
of `A` over conjugation by `{I, Z}`. On `2 × 2` matrices it keeps the diagonal and deletes the
off-diagonal entries (the `Z`-eigenbasis is the computational basis). -/
noncomputable def diagPart (A : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ :=
  (2⁻¹ : ℂ) • (A + pauliZ * A * pauliZ)

/-- `Z X Z = −X`: conjugating `X` by `Z` flips its sign (Pauli anti-commutativity). -/
theorem pauliZ_mul_pauliX_mul_pauliZ : pauliZ * pauliX * pauliZ = -pauliX := by
  ext i j
  fin_cases i <;> fin_cases j <;>
    simp [pauliX, pauliZ, Matrix.mul_apply, Fin.sum_univ_two]

/-- `Z Y Z = −Y`: conjugating `Y` by `Z` flips its sign (Pauli anti-commutativity). -/
theorem pauliZ_mul_pauliY_mul_pauliZ : pauliZ * pauliY * pauliZ = -pauliY := by
  ext i j
  fin_cases i <;> fin_cases j <;>
    simp [pauliY, pauliZ, Matrix.mul_apply, Fin.sum_univ_two]

/-- `Z Z Z = Z`: `Z` commutes with itself, so conjugation fixes it. -/
theorem pauliZ_mul_pauliZ_mul_pauliZ : pauliZ * pauliZ * pauliZ = pauliZ := by
  rw [pauliZ_mul_self, one_mul]

/-- `diagPart` is additive. -/
theorem diagPart_add (A B : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) :
    diagPart (A + B) = diagPart A + diagPart B := by
  simp only [diagPart, Matrix.mul_add, Matrix.add_mul]
  module

/-- `diagPart` is ℂ-homogeneous. -/
theorem diagPart_smul (c : ℂ) (A : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) :
    diagPart (c • A) = c • diagPart A := by
  simp only [diagPart, Matrix.mul_smul, Matrix.smul_mul]
  module

/-- The off-diagonal Pauli `X` has zero `Z`-diagonal part. -/
@[simp] theorem diagPart_pauliX : diagPart pauliX = 0 := by
  rw [diagPart, pauliZ_mul_pauliX_mul_pauliZ, add_neg_cancel, smul_zero]

/-- The off-diagonal Pauli `Y` has zero `Z`-diagonal part. -/
@[simp] theorem diagPart_pauliY : diagPart pauliY = 0 := by
  rw [diagPart, pauliZ_mul_pauliY_mul_pauliZ, add_neg_cancel, smul_zero]

/-- The diagonal Pauli `Z` is its own `Z`-diagonal part. -/
@[simp] theorem diagPart_pauliZ : diagPart pauliZ = pauliZ := by
  rw [diagPart, pauliZ_mul_pauliZ_mul_pauliZ]
  module

/-- **`Z`-diagonal part of `n·σ`.** Only the `ẑ`-component survives:
`diagPart (n·σ) = n_z • Z`. -/
theorem diagPart_pauliDot (n : Fin 3 → ℝ) :
    diagPart (pauliDot n) = (n 2 : ℂ) • pauliZ := by
  rw [pauliDot, diagPart_add, diagPart_add, diagPart_smul, diagPart_smul, diagPart_smul,
    diagPart_pauliX, diagPart_pauliY, diagPart_pauliZ, smul_zero, smul_zero, zero_add, zero_add]

/-! ### The `ẑ`-refocusing pulses and the toggling-frame average -/

/-- The `180°` `ẑ`-refocusing pulse on spin 1, `Z⊗I` (conjugation by the physical pulse `−iZ`). -/
noncomputable def refocusZ₁ : Matrix (Fin 2 × Fin 2) (Fin 2 × Fin 2) ℂ :=
  pauliZ ⊗ₖ (1 : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ)

/-- The `180°` `ẑ`-refocusing pulse on spin 2, `I⊗Z`. -/
noncomputable def refocusZ₂ : Matrix (Fin 2 × Fin 2) (Fin 2 × Fin 2) ℂ :=
  (1 : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) ⊗ₖ pauliZ

/-- The joint `180°` `ẑ`-pulse on both spins, `Z⊗Z` — the product of the two single-spin pulses. -/
noncomputable def refocusZ₁₂ : Matrix (Fin 2 × Fin 2) (Fin 2 × Fin 2) ℂ :=
  pauliZ ⊗ₖ pauliZ

/-- The joint pulse is the composite of the two single-spin pulses: `(Z⊗I)(I⊗Z) = Z⊗Z`. -/
theorem refocusZ₁_mul_refocusZ₂ : refocusZ₁ * refocusZ₂ = refocusZ₁₂ := by
  rw [refocusZ₁, refocusZ₂, refocusZ₁₂, ← Matrix.mul_kronecker_mul, one_mul, mul_one]

/-- The **toggling-frame (zeroth-order average) Hamiltonian** produced by the `ẑ`-refocusing pulse
cycle: the symmetric average of `H` over conjugation by the four pulses `{I⊗I, Z⊗I, I⊗Z, Z⊗Z}`. -/
noncomputable def zRefocusAverage (H : Matrix (Fin 2 × Fin 2) (Fin 2 × Fin 2) ℂ) :
    Matrix (Fin 2 × Fin 2) (Fin 2 × Fin 2) ℂ :=
  (4⁻¹ : ℂ) • (H + refocusZ₁ * H * refocusZ₁ + refocusZ₂ * H * refocusZ₂
    + refocusZ₁₂ * H * refocusZ₁₂)

/-- `zRefocusAverage` is additive. -/
theorem zRefocusAverage_add (H K : Matrix (Fin 2 × Fin 2) (Fin 2 × Fin 2) ℂ) :
    zRefocusAverage (H + K) = zRefocusAverage H + zRefocusAverage K := by
  simp only [zRefocusAverage, Matrix.mul_add, Matrix.add_mul]
  module

/-- `zRefocusAverage` is ℂ-homogeneous. -/
theorem zRefocusAverage_smul (c : ℂ) (H : Matrix (Fin 2 × Fin 2) (Fin 2 × Fin 2) ℂ) :
    zRefocusAverage (c • H) = c • zRefocusAverage H := by
  simp only [zRefocusAverage, Matrix.mul_smul, Matrix.smul_mul]
  module

/-- `zRefocusAverage` subtracts. -/
theorem zRefocusAverage_sub (H K : Matrix (Fin 2 × Fin 2) (Fin 2 × Fin 2) ℂ) :
    zRefocusAverage (H - K) = zRefocusAverage H - zRefocusAverage K := by
  simp only [zRefocusAverage, Matrix.mul_sub, Matrix.sub_mul]
  module

/-- **Structural identity.** On a Kronecker product the toggling-frame average factors into the
single-spin `Z`-diagonal parts: `⟨A⊗B⟩ = diagPart A ⊗ diagPart B`. (Conjugating `A⊗B` by `Z⊗I`,
`I⊗Z`, `Z⊗Z` gives `ZAZ⊗B`, `A⊗ZBZ`, `ZAZ⊗ZBZ`, and `¼(A+ZAZ)⊗(B+ZBZ)` is the claimed product.) -/
theorem zRefocusAverage_kronecker (A B : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) :
    zRefocusAverage (A ⊗ₖ B) = diagPart A ⊗ₖ diagPart B := by
  simp only [zRefocusAverage, refocusZ₁, refocusZ₂, refocusZ₁₂, diagPart,
    ← Matrix.mul_kronecker_mul, one_mul, mul_one, Matrix.smul_kronecker, Matrix.kronecker_smul,
    Matrix.add_kronecker, Matrix.kronecker_add]
  module

/-! ### Averaging the dipolar coupling -/

/-- The isotropic coupling refocuses to `Z⊗Z`: of `σ⃗₁·σ⃗₂ = X⊗X + Y⊗Y + Z⊗Z` only the diagonal
`Z⊗Z` term survives (`diagPart X = diagPart Y = 0`, `diagPart Z = Z`). -/
theorem zRefocusAverage_spinSpinCoupling :
    zRefocusAverage spinSpinCoupling = pauliZ ⊗ₖ pauliZ := by
  rw [spinSpinCoupling, Fin.sum_univ_three, pauliSigma_zero, pauliSigma_one, pauliSigma_two,
    zRefocusAverage_add, zRefocusAverage_add, zRefocusAverage_kronecker, zRefocusAverage_kronecker,
    zRefocusAverage_kronecker, diagPart_pauliX, diagPart_pauliY, diagPart_pauliZ,
    Matrix.zero_kronecker, add_zero, zero_add]

/-- The anisotropic coupling refocuses to `n_z² • (Z⊗Z)`: `(σ⃗₁·n̂)(σ⃗₂·n̂) = (n·σ)⊗(n·σ)` and
`diagPart (n·σ) = n_z Z`, so `⟨(n·σ)⊗(n·σ)⟩ = (n_z Z)⊗(n_z Z) = n_z² (Z⊗Z)`. -/
theorem zRefocusAverage_spinDirProduct (n : Fin 3 → ℝ) :
    zRefocusAverage (spinDirProduct n) = ((n 2 : ℂ) ^ 2) • (pauliZ ⊗ₖ pauliZ) := by
  rw [spinDirProduct, zRefocusAverage_kronecker, diagPart_pauliDot, Matrix.smul_kronecker,
    Matrix.kronecker_smul, smul_smul, ← pow_two]

/-- The dipolar bracket refocuses to `(1 − 3 n_z²) • (Z⊗Z)`: `⟨σ⃗₁·σ⃗₂ − 3(σ⃗₁·n̂)(σ⃗₂·n̂)⟩
= Z⊗Z − 3 n_z² (Z⊗Z)`. -/
theorem zRefocusAverage_dipolarBracket (n : Fin 3 → ℝ) :
    zRefocusAverage (dipolarBracket n) = (1 - 3 * (n 2 : ℂ) ^ 2) • (pauliZ ⊗ₖ pauliZ) := by
  rw [dipolarBracket, zRefocusAverage_sub, zRefocusAverage_smul, zRefocusAverage_spinSpinCoupling,
    zRefocusAverage_spinDirProduct, smul_smul]
  module

/-- The **residual (secular) dipolar coupling constant** `J_eff = γ₁ γ₂ (1 − 3 n_z²) / r³` left
after the `ẑ`-refocusing pulse sequence (the `∝ (1 − 3 cos²θ)` scaling of the dipolar coupling). -/
noncomputable def dipolarEffectiveCoupling (γ₁ γ₂ r : ℝ) (n : Fin 3 → ℝ) : ℝ :=
  γ₁ * γ₂ * (1 - 3 * (n 2) ^ 2) / r ^ 3

/-- **Nielsen & Chuang, Exercise 7.40 (refocusing dipolar interactions).** The `ẑ`-refocusing pulse
sequence turns the through-space dipolar coupling `H^D_{1,2}(n̂)` into the simple weak-coupling form
of (7.138): its toggling-frame average Hamiltonian is `(ℏ J_eff / 4) • Z₁Z₂`, a pure `Z₁Z₂`
interaction with effective constant `J_eff = γ₁ γ₂ (1 − 3 n_z²) / r³`, for every choice of the
physical constants `γ₁, γ₂, ℏ, r` and every internuclear direction `n̂`. -/
theorem zRefocusAverage_dipolarCoupling (γ₁ γ₂ ℏ r : ℝ) (n : Fin 3 → ℝ) :
    zRefocusAverage (dipolarCoupling γ₁ γ₂ ℏ r n)
      = ((ℏ * dipolarEffectiveCoupling γ₁ γ₂ r n / 4 : ℝ) : ℂ) • (pauliZ ⊗ₖ pauliZ) := by
  rw [dipolarCoupling, zRefocusAverage_smul, zRefocusAverage_dipolarBracket, smul_smul]
  congr 1
  simp only [dipolarEffectiveCoupling]
  push_cast
  ring

end AxQM.Concrete
